Our mission at the Department of Chemistry, Materials and Chemical Engineering "Giulio Natta" is:
- to conduct high-quality research in the fields of chemistry, chemical engineering, science and materials engineering and bioengineering, promoting their central role in all the new technologies involvingmatter and energy transformation;
- to raise, in an intellectually stimulating environment, students aspiring to undertake technical-scientific careers in industry, university, government or as entrepreneurs; this reflects, among other things, in the substantial contributionof Department's faculty membersto teaching in all University's Schools, with particular reference to Chemical Engineering Bachelor Degree and Master Degrees in Biomedical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Materials Engineering and Nanotechnology and Safety and Prevention Engineering in the Process Industry;
- to support the Country's development through technology transfer between academia, industry and government agencies 
The Department of Chemistry, Materials and Chemical Engineering "Giulio Natta"aims at being recognized as a leading institution on a local, national and international level:
- for the excellence of its research, at the frontier of chemistry, materials, chemical engineering and bioengineering;
- as a promoter of innovation and sustainable, knowledge-driven growth;
- as an education pole for highly qualified and responsible professionals;
- as an international point of convergence for students, researchers and university professors, to become a fully multi-cultural and multi-national institution.

T FORMA is a training center accredited from the Sicily Region. The courses are delivered in different ways (e.g. e-learning and webinar) and for the following areas:

- Job Security;
- certified training;
- nutrition;
- school education;
- bachelor/master's degree;
- Mother Tongue Language courses;
- Formation 4.0;
- Industry 4.0.

T FORMA also offers specialized consultancy services and supports companies to access public funds intended for supporting entrepreneurial initiatives: lost funding, funded financing and tax credit. T FORMA therefore offers advice on Italian and European funding calls.

